{"title":"2014 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 1c","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Lisa earns two times as much per hour as Bart. Lisa works 6 hours and Bart works 4 hours. They earn $200 in total. How much does Lisa earn per hour?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/0/420696c72b7a967573a4025803a5baaeb6d42c84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"16\" /> be the amount that Bart earns per hour. Since Lisa earns two times as much per hour as Bart, Lisa earns <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/d/e2da263951b52d9d21c9e5ddf287b5e361501194.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$2b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> per hour.\n</p><p>Since Lisa works <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hours, Lisa earns <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/9/6c944c084272ba1deba662fc69a52de74945a5e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$2b \\times 6 = \\$12b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"118\" height=\"17\" /> in total. \n</p><p>Since Bart works <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hours, Bart earns <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/c/25ccddc7391cc98ec8620b322f017c39233ed712.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$4b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> in total.\n</p><p>Thus, altogether, they earn <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/1/091503df5809544bf0b4e1563a1e954e730a1ae1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$12b + \\$4b = \\$16b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"144\" height=\"17\" />. This is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/0/4a0d1ea2f817036d72f6d1449562fc3a1dfd01da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/7/2377910fabe1da4d5df8b70582acd7a97a561f85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$16b = \\$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"98\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/c/ecc7fa25c1947a15051169b379e25c4b8aa1ac2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\frac{\\$200}{\\$16} = 12.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"131\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Lisa earns <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times this, so Lisa earns <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/c/23c98a6f85f934cce1015dc0e3f800c2b385e71e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12.5 \\times 2 = \\boxed{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"119\" height=\"25\" /> dollars per hour.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/9/f9975d9fe7f9df3b69dba1ad4d555b609943f058.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$l$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" /> be the amount that Bart earns per hour. Since Lisa earns two times as much per hour as Bart, Bart earns <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/0/810271742a7de18f301a6900020359d1c0e3d1a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$\\frac{l}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"39\" /> per hour.\n</p><p>Since Lisa works <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hours, Lisa earns <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/5/395b028b8252084bb7e548bf04b38c4fc2247e88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$6l$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"16\" /> in total.\n</p><p>Since Bart works <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hours, Bart earns <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/6/126edfa83779d4cd04a5588f50f26bf6fbc95e01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$\\frac{l}{2} \\times 4 = \\$2l$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"104\" height=\"39\" /> in total.\n</p><p>Thus, altogether, they earn <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b7732edfadf9e413b6e8847167c59ddfc170f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$6l + \\$2l = \\$8l$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"120\" height=\"17\" />. This is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/0/4a0d1ea2f817036d72f6d1449562fc3a1dfd01da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/1/151eb6fa7b9307c491e37449eacb0cdf30cdabe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$8l = \\$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/b/d4bd0277b5aaa136025fc5b259c64e159c4ff238.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l = \\frac{\\$200}{\\$8} = \\boxed{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"126\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017234314\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.032 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 108/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 78/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4000/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.310      1 2015_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1\n100.00%    6.310      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36022:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017234314 and revision id 279641. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}